From 0e4918d9dae0ccc1fb68422012aec4f37f98d195 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hibreak <build@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:06:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sf: optionally send the client target's damage to the
 composer

HWC2 setClientTarget() always got an empty damage list ("whole buffer"),
see the TODO in Display::setClientTarget. With
debug.sf.hwc_client_target_damage=1 the frame's dirty region (mapped
from layer-stack to framebuffer space) is attached to the GPU-composed
buffer as surface damage, and FramebufferSurface forwards it to the HAL.

The MT6877 e-ink composer on the Bigme HiBreak Pro, which we drive with
forced client composition, uses this damage for partial panel updates.
Without it every frame, even a single keyboard key press, refreshes the
whole screen.

Change-Id: I4315baf97b4d1699d17fc0b5923801a54e81adc9
---
